  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Steam & Deep Cleaning</p>
      <h1>Professional steam and deep cleaning for businesses</h1>
      <p class="lead">Some build-up needs more than daily upkeep. MSNA Cleaning & Support offers targeted intensive cleaning for suitable surfaces in washrooms, kitchens, staff areas, business premises and certain workshop zones. We choose the method based on the surface, the build-up and the safety conditions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Where can steam cleaning help?</h2></div>
      <ul class="info-list"><li><b>Washrooms:</b> suitable wall tiles, grout and selected fittings.</li><li><b>Staff kitchens:</b> certain hard, heat-resistant surfaces and localised build-up.</li><li><b>Showrooms and offices:</b> spot treatment of pre-approved hard surfaces.</li><li><b>Workshops:</b> only suitable zones, after checking machinery, oil and electrical risks.</li><li><b>Handovers:</b> detail treatment where temperature and moisture can be safely applied.</li></ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section style="border-top:1px solid var(--line-soft);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>What is the difference between steam and deep cleaning?</h2></div>
      <p class="lead">Steam cleaning uses heat and moisture to loosen build-up on suitable materials. Deep cleaning is a broader, more intensive approach that can also involve mechanical cleaning, adapted products, rinsing and drying. Not every deep clean uses steam.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section style="border-top:1px solid var(--line-soft);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Our six-step approach</h2></div>
      <div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="n">01</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">We assess the location, the level of build-up and the safety risks.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="n">02</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">We check suitability against material and manufacturer instructions.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="n">03</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">Where appropriate, we test on an inconspicuous spot.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="n">04</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">We mark out the work zone and protect sensitive objects.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="n">05</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">We clean in a controlled way and remove loosened build-up.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="n">06</div><div><p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-dim);">We check the visible result and advise on drying and ventilation.</p></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section style="border-top:1px solid var(--line-soft);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Important limitations</h2></div>
      <div class="callout"><p>Steam is not automatically used on unprotected electrical installations, sensitive electronics, heat- or moisture-sensitive upholstery, unknown coatings or fragile surfaces. A material check always comes first. We do not promise guaranteed disinfection or a microbiological result without a separately validated process.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
